@rainj-me Following up on my September 28 request: could you review the endpoint placement for the SageMaker portion of #23206, item 25, or point me to the right Rust-server reviewer?

This adds `/ping` and `/invocations` through the existing chat handler. The PR records 275 passing CPU tests, with three Linux `/dev/shm` cases excluded after confirming the same failures on the unchanged macOS baseline. Real-model serving and AWS SageMaker deployment have not been validated.

CI is still missing `run-ci`, and the branch needs updating for #21065's minimum base before a fresh run. The separate coverage-based test-selector failure was a GitHub API HTTP 503. Could you help review the approach and authorize the relevant checks once the branch is updated? Thanks!

